prompt:
Use the image generation tool. Make ONE PNG, 2048 wide by 1024 tall: hair color variants of the SAME heroine head and ponytail parts.

Reference 1 shows the original HEAD (left, facing right in 3/4 view, with a hair bun and red hair tie) and the separate PONYTAIL part (right). Reference 2 is the full part sheet for style. Match the exact pixel-art look (hard-edged 16-bit pixel art, chunky square pixels about 4 output pixels wide, limited palette, dark outline, no antialiasing, no gradients).

CRITICAL: keep the FACE exactly the same as reference 1: same East Asian face, same warm skin tone, same dark brown eyes with white highlight, same dark eyebrows and eyelashes, same mouth, same dark brown outline around face and hair. ONLY the hair strands (bangs, side locks, bun, ponytail) change color. Keep the red hair tie red. Same size and pose as reference 1.

Background: flat solid pure magenta #FF00FF, no checkerboard, no text, no grid lines. Layout: 4 columns by 2 rows, pieces fully isolated with padding, never touching. Row 1: four HEADS; row 2: the matching four PONYTAILS directly below each head. Column order:
 1. jet BLACK hair with subtle blue-grey highlights;
 2. SILVER-WHITE hair (cool light grey with white highlights and medium grey shadows; outlines stay dark), face and eyes unchanged, eyebrows stay dark grey-brown;
 3. deep AUBURN red-brown hair;
 4. dark CHESTNUT brown with a single white streak.

Use the image generation tool. Make ONE PNG, 1536 wide by 1024 tall: FIVE different TROUSER designs for a Spine skeletal rig of a small chibi wuxia heroine, each split into a THIGH part and a CALF part that must join cleanly.

Reference 1 shows the current THIGH part (left) and CALF part (right). Reference 2 shows them ASSEMBLED on the character in the game: a short slanted thigh, a very SHORT calf, and a big separate boot below. Reference 3 is the full part sheet for style. Match the exact pixel-art look (hard-edged 16-bit pixel art, chunky square pixels about 4 output pixels wide, limited palette, 1-2 pixel dark brown outline, no antialiasing, no gradients).

Rules so the parts join cleanly on the rig:
- THIGH: drawn pointing straight DOWN, hip at top (a round covered cap), same chunky width as reference 1. Its BOTTOM ends in a clean horizontal knee CUFF or band of cloth. The knee is always covered by cloth, a knee pad or wrapping, never bare skin.
- CALF: drawn pointing straight DOWN, about 60 percent of the thigh length (short and chunky like reference 1, NOT as long as the thigh), NO round cap at the top: its top edge is plain fabric that will be hidden under the thigh cuff. Its bottom ends in a narrow gathered cuff or wrap at the ankle that tucks into a boot. NO foot and NO shoe.
- Both parts of a design have the same width at the knee so they look continuous.

Designs (clearly different silhouettes, not just colors):
1. tight black LEGGINGS with criss-cross leather binding straps, slim;
2. loose WHITE LINEN trousers, baggy on the thigh, gathered with a blue band at the ankle;
3. ARMORED: dark trousers with a steel lamellar thigh guard and a steel shin greave with leather straps, a round steel knee cop covering the knee;
4. brown knee-length breeches whose cuff covers the knee, and a calf tightly WRAPPED in cream cloth puttee bandages from knee to ankle (no bare skin showing);
5. brown hunter's leather leggings with FUR trim at the knee cuff and at the ankle.

Layout on flat solid pure magenta #FF00FF, no grid lines, no text: 5 columns (designs 1 to 5, left to right) by 2 rows. Row 1: the five THIGH parts. Row 2: the matching five CALF parts directly below. Every part fully isolated with padding, never touching another part.
